WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.000
Most boat fires are preventable, and prevention is plain housekeeping.

2
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.950
Keep the bilges clean, with no oil or fuel in them.

3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.825
A clean bilge also shows you a new leak right away.

4
00:00:13.075 --> 00:00:19.300
Inspect the fuel lines, hose clamps, tank vents and tanks for chafe, corrosion and weeping.

5
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.775
Store oily rags, paints and solvents in proper containers.

6
00:00:24.025 --> 00:00:28.800
An oily rag wadded up in a locker can heat up and light all by itself.

7
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.800
Allow smoking only where it’s safe, if you allow it at all.

8
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:41.000
And remember that a few minutes of looking at the dock is far easier than fighting a fire offshore with six passengers aboard.

9
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.875
That’s lesson four.

10
00:00:44.125 --> 00:00:45.850
Vapor sinks.

11
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.450
Close up to fuel, open up to start, four minutes on the blower.

12
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.575
Carbon monoxide looks like seasickness.

13
00:00:53.825 --> 00:00:56.475
And nobody swims near shore power.

14
00:00:56.725 --> 00:00:59.525
Next time: what keeps a boat upright.
